===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A company whose products are [[widespread]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Robert Metcalfe|title=Microsoft and Netscape open some new fronts in escalating Web Wars|work=InfoWorld|date=August 21, 1995|volume=17|issue=34|page=35|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_0joEAAAAMBAJ/page/n42/mode/1up|passage=After its phenomenal stock offering two weeks ago, Netscape Communications Corp. is well on its way to becoming the '''Microsoft''' of the Internet.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Daniel Charles|title=Lords of the Harvest: Biotech, Big Money, and the Future of Food|isbn=0738202916|page=110|passage=Similarly, said Fraley, farmers were going to demand Bt cotton or Roundup-resistant soybean plants no matter where they went shopping for seeds. Monsanto would be the '''Microsoft''' of agriculture.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|author=Merrill Goozner|title=The $800 Million Pill: The Truth Behind the Cost of New Drugs|isbn=0520246705|page=64|passage=The company wanted to turn Celera into the '''Microsoft''' of the gene-hunting world, selling its version of the human genome to private or public gene hunters through a proprietary computer program.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Andrew Beaujon|title=Body Piercing Saved My Life: Inside the Phenomenon of Christian Rock|isbn=0306814579|page=232|passage=Shepherding is more or less gone (though there’s an interesting move back toward discipleship in today’s church especially among those influenced by Rick Warren’s blockbuster book ''The Purpose-Driven Life''), but Integrity remains as sort of the '''Microsoft''' of worship music.}}

